3,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-28T19:44:35Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T19:49:15Z","body":"@Ivorforce We have reviewed this on animation meeting yesterday, and @lyuma reviewed the code after meeting.\r\n\r\nMost of it is a duplicate of existing code (makima is a modified version of the cubic formula), and the main thing to be careful about is the refactoring change parts, but it was mentioned above by @lyuma.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5877209289/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5879202396","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123835#issuecomment-5879202396","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123835","id":5879202396,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXm2CXA","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-28T21:36:47Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T21:37:39Z","body":"Alright, that's fine then. I couldn't make it out from the approval since neither approval mentioned a code review or opened code threads, so it looked like nobody had reviewed it.\r\n\r\nThere seems to be a lot of code and methods added to core too. Normally we'd [prefer local solutions](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/engine/best_practices.html#prefer-local-solutions), so this ending up in core is a bit unusual.\r\n\r\nThe interpolation looks nice and seems to solve a real problem, but as far as I'm seeing, nobody's asking for the interpolation methods themselves to be exposed. \r\n\r\nIf you think these methods should be exposed, I think this should to be discussed with the core team.\r\nOtherwise, I'd propose to remove them from core, add them to the animation folders instead, and simply use them from there without exposing anything on `Vector3` etc.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5879202396/reactions","total_count":1,"+1