5,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcsurAQ","user":{"login":"GNSS-Stylist","id":50438441,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDM4NDQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50438441?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GNSS-Stylist","html_url":"https://github.com/GNSS-Stylist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GNSS-Stylist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GNSS-Stylist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GNSS-Stylist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GNSS-Stylist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GNSS-Stylist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GNSS-Stylist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GNSS-Stylist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GNSS-Stylist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GNSS-Stylist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-16T17:21:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T17:22:13Z","body":"Thanks for this! Sometimes cubic interpolation's overshoot can be very annoying and makima seems to fix it. Used makima for both movement and rotation (quaternions) when making this short video (=playing animation in Godot):\r\nhttps://www.youtube.com/shorts/offXGAUu0DE\r\nIn this case differences to cubic interpolation are especially noticeable when starting to move/turn and stopping. Both of these cases cause overshoot (or rather pre/post-movement/turning) with cubic.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6220917505/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]